Feature:

Background: This executes once per feature file
	Given these properties
		|portal.release|false|
		|portal.upstream|false|
		|custom.properties|default.layout.template.id=1_column|
		|testray.main.component.name|Adaptive Media|

Setup: This executes before each scenario 
	Given TestCase set Up Portal Instance
	When User first Login PG

Teardown: This executes after each scenario 
	Given these variables
		|testPortalInstance|TestPropsUtil#get('test.portal.instance')|
Scenario: Add AMI With High Density Resolution
Priority: 5
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|addHighDensityDisplay|true|
		|imageName|Low Resolution|
		|maxHeight|480|
		|maxWidth|320|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Low Resolution|
		|maxHeight|480|
		|maxWidth|320|
		|percentAdapted|0|
	Then AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Low Resolution-2x|
		|maxHeight|960|
		|maxWidth|640|
		|percentAdapted|0|
Scenario: Add And Edit Entries With Special Characters
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz|
		|maxHeight|25|
		|maxWidth|25|
	And AdaptiveMedia edit Image Resolution
		|imageName|abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz|
		|imageNameEdit|ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ|
	And AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|1234567890!@#$%^&*()~`|
		|maxHeight|75|
		|maxWidth|75|
	Then AdaptiveMedia edit Image Resolution
		|imageName|1234567890!@#$%^&*()~`|
		|imageNameEdit|[]\{}|:";',./><?|
Scenario: Add And Update AMI With Images In DM
Priority: 5
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|Low Resolution|
		|maxHeight|480|
		|maxWidth|320|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Low Resolution|
		|maxHeight|480|
		|maxWidth|320|
		|percentAdapted|0|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Content
		|portlet|Documents and Media|
	And DMDocument add CP
		|dmDocumentDescription|DM Document Description|
		|dmDocumentFile|Document_1.jpg|
		|dmDocumentTitle|Document_1.jpg|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	And AdaptiveMedia adapt Remaining Images
		|imageName|Low Resolution|
		|percentAdapted|100|
	And AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|High Resolution|
		|maxHeight|1280|
		|maxWidth|1440|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|High Resolution|
		|maxHeight|1280|
		|maxWidth|1440|
		|percentAdapted|0|
	And AdaptiveMedia select Adaptive Media Image
		|imageName|High Resolution|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Number Of Adapted Images
		|numberOfAdaptedImages|0/1|
	And AdaptiveMedia edit Image Resolution
		|imageName|High Resolution|
		|imageNameEdit|High Resolution Edited|
		|maxHeightEdit|1080|
		|maxWidthEdit|1920|
	And AdaptiveMedia select Adaptive Media Image
		|imageName|High Resolution Edited|
	Then AdaptiveMedia view Number Of Adapted Images
		|numberOfAdaptedImages|0/1|
Scenario: Add Duplicate Image Resolution
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|customID|custom-id|
		|imageName|Image Variant With Custom ID|
		|maxHeight|350|
		|maxWidth|450|
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	And AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|customID|custom-id|
		|duplicate|true|
		|imageName|Image Variant With Duplicate Custom ID|
		|maxHeight|350|
		|maxWidth|450|
	And Navigator open URL
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	Then AdaptiveMedia view No Image Resolution
Scenario: Add Image Variants For Blog Entry
Priority: 5
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|100|
		|maxWidth|100|
	And AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|Large Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|1000|
		|maxWidth|1000|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|100|
		|maxWidth|100|
		|percentAdapted|0|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Large Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|1000|
		|maxWidth|1000|
		|percentAdapted|0|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Content
		|portlet|Documents and Media|
	And DMDocument add CP
		|dmDocumentDescription|Adaptive Media Image Description|
		|dmDocumentFile|high_resolution_photo.jpg|
		|dmDocumentTitle|high_resolution_photo.jpg|
	And Pause at locator '3000'
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	And AdaptiveMedia adapt Remaining Images
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|percentAdapted|100|
	And AdaptiveMedia adapt Remaining Images
		|imageName|Large Image Variant|
		|percentAdapted|100|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|100|
		|maxWidth|100|
		|percentAdapted|100|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Large Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|1000|
		|maxWidth|1000|
		|percentAdapted|100|
	And ProductMenu goto Sites Content
		|portlet|Blogs|
	And BlogsNavigator goto Add Entry
	And BlogsEntry add Title
		|entryTitle|Blogs Entry With Adaptive Media Image|
	And ItemSelector goto Item Selector Via Alloy Editor
	And ItemSelector select DM Image
		|imageFileName|high_resolution_photo.jpg|
	And Pause at locator '2000'
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Variant URL
		|imageName|high_resolution_photo.jpg|
	Then Button click Publish
Scenario: Cannot Add Non Numeric Width Or Height
Priority: 5
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Non Numeric Image Resolution
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|notallowed|
		|maxWidth|notallowed|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	Then AssertElementPresent at locator 'Message#EMPTY_INFO'
Scenario: Edit And Delete Disabled AMI
Priority: 5
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|maxHeight|100|
		|maxWidth|100|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|imageState|Enabled|
		|maxHeight|100|
		|maxWidth|100|
		|percentAdapted|0|
	And AdaptiveMedia disable Image Resolution
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|imageState|Disabled|
	And AdaptiveMedia edit Image Resolution
		|imageName|Small Image Variant|
		|imageNameEdit|Large Image Variant|
		|maxHeightEdit|1000|
		|maxWidthEdit|1000|
	And AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|Large Image Variant|
		|imageState|Disabled|
		|maxHeight|1000|
		|maxWidth|1000|
		|percentAdapted|0|
	Then AdaptiveMedia delete Image Resolution
		|imageName|Large Image Variant|
