Scenario: View Image Resolution Across Sites
Priority: 4
	Given ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	When AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|This should appear on a new site|
		|maxHeight|400|
		|maxWidth|300|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Sites
		|portlet|Sites|
	And Site add Blank CP
		|siteName|New Site with AM|
	And ProductMenu goto Site
		|site|New Site with AM|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	Then AdaptiveMedia view Image Resolution Table Entry
		|imageName|This should appear on a new site|
		|maxHeight|400|
		|maxWidth|300|
		|percentAdapted|0|
Scenario: View No Image Resolution In New Virtual Instance
Priority: 4
	Given these properties
		|test.name.skip.portal.instance|AdaptiveMedia#ViewNoImageResolutionInNewVirtualInstance|
	When ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Virtual Instances|
	And PortalInstances add CP
		|mailDomain|www.able.com|
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
		|webId|www.able.com|
	And PortalInstances view CP
		|virtualHost|www.able.com|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	And AdaptiveMedia add Image Resolution
		|imageName|This should not appear on new virtual instance|
		|maxHeight|300|
		|maxWidth|300|
	And User first Login PG
		|password|test|
		|userEmailAddress|test@www.able.com|
		|virtualHostsURL|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And Navigator open Specific URL
		|url|http://www.able.com:8080|
	And ProductMenu goto Control Panel Configuration
		|portlet|Adaptive Media|
	Then AdaptiveMedia view No Image Resolution
		|imageName|This should not appear on new virtual instance|
